    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0529" n="1363" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659a.119/14</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-22T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 23, 3.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10185. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 626. After several weeks conferences between Allied Governments and Iceland
                    delegates, at which I was present or represented, an agreement has been reached
                    between British, French and Italians on one side and Icelanders covering in
                    detail the points summarized below.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
